/* §7.63: `Array<T>` is an ALIAS and now HAS an emission, but a generic name
 * that is not `Array` still does not — and `Box<String>` is the one that
 * matters. §7.63 says an object argument ERASES to the bare class (`Box *`) and
 * a non-object one is MONOMORPHISED from the declaration; neither is written.
 * Emitting the bare name would drop the argument, the fact that it had one, and
 * the element type with it. */
class RefuseGenericArgument: Object {
    property items: Box<String>
}
